{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git log --format='%h %s%n%b' 319bfd9c..7e2b4a3e -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_ledger_memo.go; rg -n 'type ReviewAttestation struct|type ReviewAttestationsRead|type ReviewExecutionSafety|type DelegationRoutingRecord|type ReviewRunProvenance' pose-mcp/internal/pose; sed -n '368,435p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\"","aggregated_output":"604a6363 fix(pose): keep ledger refusals visible and attribute every producer\nRound 3 review findings. N1: a refused transcript check after the view was\nfinalized returned no problem, read as an intact transcript; it now reports\nthat the transcript cannot be inspected. N2: a refused header read became an\nempty observation and the bundle vanished without a loss; it is a read error\nagain. N3: a kept value was attributed only to the producer that computed it;\nthe key now carries the producer and project, so each producer reads once\nthrough the view and the final audit attributes every consumer.\n\nPOSE-Spec: pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfqwBXh8UdZwnt129jD\n\n1995df71 fix(pose): serve a kept ledger value only while the view is open\nRound 2 review finding F4: a memo hit skipped the view's lifecycle check, so\na store kept past its operation got the kept records after the view was\nfinalized. The memo now calls the view's begin before serving or computing,\nand a finalized view refuses as a read does.\n\nPOSE-Spec: pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfqwBXh8UdZwnt129jD\n\n2bf2adf1 fix(pose): compute each ledger memo once and give callers deep copies\nRound 1 review findings. F1: concurrent misses of one key both computed;\neach key now has a cell computed under sync.Once. F2: callers got shallow\ncopies sharing nested slices and pointers with the kept values; they now\nget deep copies, ReviewRun's unexported fields copied by name under a\nreflection test. F3: copying onto nil turned empty slices into nil; the\ndeep copy keeps nil and empty apart.\n\nPOSE-Spec: pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfqwBXh8UdZwnt129jD\n\n2fd7c35f perf(pose): read the review ledger once per read-view operation\nA first closeout call on harne8 read pose-dist's review ledger 280 times,\nits attestations 304 times, every bundle header on each listing, and\nchecked transcript digests 29,680 times. Within one operation the read view\nreturns the same bytes for the same read, so the parsed runs, the\nattestations per bundle filter, each bundle header and each transcript\ncheck are kept for the life of the operation. CPU of the call: 130 s -> 53 s.\n\nPOSE-Spec: pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfqwBXh8UdZwnt129jD\n\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:386:type ReviewAttestation struct {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3330:type ReviewAttestationsRead struct {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_routing.go:63:type DelegationRoutingRecord struct {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go:66:type ReviewExecutionSafety struct {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go:36:type ReviewRunProvenancePolicy struct {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go:40:type ReviewRunProvenance struct {\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) audit() governanceReadViewAudit {\n\tresult := governanceReadViewAudit{ChangedProducers: map[string]bool{}, UnknownProducers: map[string][]string{}}\n\tif op == nil {\n\t\treturn result\n\t}\n\top.mu.Lock()\n\troots := append([]*governanceReadViewRoot(nil), op.roots...)\n\tinitialRoots := op.initialRoots // Immutable after beginGovernanceReadView returns.\n\tinitialConflicts := op.initialConflicts\n\tcurrentRoots := op.currentRoots\n\top.mu.Unlock()\n\tperRoot := map[*governanceReadView]governanceReadViewAudit{}\n\tauditBudget := &governanceReadViewAuditBudget{}\n\tfor _, root := range roots {\n\t\tif _, done := perRoot[root.view]; done {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tperRoot[root.view] = root.view.auditSingleWithBudget(auditBudget)\n\t}\n\tchanged := []string{}\n\tfor _, audit := range perRoot {\n\t\tchanged = append(changed, audit.ChangedPaths...)\n\t\tfor producer, value := range audit.ChangedProducers {\n\t\t\tresult.ChangedProducers[producer] = value\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor producer, reasons := range audit.UnknownProducers {\n\t\t\tresult.UnknownProducers[producer] = append(result.UnknownProducers[producer], reasons...)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif op.git != nil {\n\t\tgitAudit := op.git.audit()\n\t\tprimaryAudit := perRoot[op.primary]\n\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&primaryAudit, gitAudit)\n\t\tperRoot[op.primary] = primaryAudit\n\t\tchanged = append(changed, gitAudit.ChangedPaths...)\n\t\tfor producer, value := range gitAudit.ChangedProducers {\n\t\t\tresult.ChangedProducers[producer] = value\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor producer, reasons := range gitAudit.UnknownProducers {\n\t\t\tresult.UnknownProducers[producer] = append(result.UnknownProducers[producer], reasons...)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif currentRoots != nil {\n\t\tcurrent, conflicts, overBudget := currentRoots()\n\t\tif overBudget || !sameStringMap(initialRoots, current) || !sameBoolMap(initialConflicts, conflicts) {\n\t\t\tregistryAudit := governanceReadViewAudit{UnknownProducers: map[string][]string{}}\n\t\t\treason := \"authorized root registry changed during the operation\"\n\t\t\tif overBudget {\n\t\t\t\treason = \"authorized root registry exceeded its bounded final-audit budget\"\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tregistryAudit.ChangedPaths = []string{\"authorized-roots\"}\n\t\t\t\tregistryAudit.ChangedProducers = map[string]bool{\"projection\": true}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tregistryAudit.UnknownProducers[\"projection\"] = []string{reason}\n\t\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&result, registryAudit)\n\t\t\tchanged = append(changed, registryAudit.ChangedPaths...)\n\t\t\t// Metadata and the captured proof are assembled from these root\n\t\t\t// audits. Keep the operation-wide registry observation on the\n\t\t\t// primary root too, so it cannot disappear after the bounded retry.\n\t\t\tprimaryAudit := perRoot[op.primary]\n\t\t\tmergeGovernanceReadViewAudit(&primaryAudit, registryAudit)\n\t\t\tperRoot[op.primary] = primaryAudit\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tresult.ChangedPaths = uniqueSorted(changed)\n\tfor producer := range result.UnknownProducers {\n\t\tresult.UnknownProducers[producer] = uniqueSorted(result.UnknownProducers[producer])\n\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
